Chapter: PigsSpec
  cites Foreword chapter ListUtils
  cites Foreword chapter Console
  cites Safari chapter Critter
  cites Safari chapter Pigs
  cites Judge chapter Grade

 Pigs: the one the rider gawks at, the seven-by-seven herd behind it, and the two
 straight ranks that are not worth gawking at.

 THREE POPULATIONS AND THEY ARE NOT INTERCHANGEABLE. `gaze-pig` is a single
 animal placed so the head-turn always aims at a pig that is actually drawn;
 `fill-pig-herd` is forty-nine on a sheared grid; `fill-pig-row` is ten in two
 straight ranks with NO jitter at all. Their counts and their shapes are what
 tell them apart, and a chapter that fed the gaze at a herd pig would still draw
 the same field.

 THE ROWS ARE GRADED AT THE JITTER'S BOUND, as in HerdSpec, and here the along
 axis is the tighter of the two: columns are 4 metres apart against a jitter of
 at most 1.2, so the bands are 1.6 clear. Across is 6 apart against 1.0. The row
 shear -- each row is 6 further along as well as 6 further off -- is what slants
 the herd's sides, and it shows up as the whole along band moving with the row.

 THE STRAIGHT RANKS CARRY NO SINE, so they are graded at 0.0. That is worth
 having beside the herd: it is the same chapter placing animals, and the one
 population where every coordinate is exact.

 A route length of 1000 puts the base at 940, and every value below lands on a
 whole number of metres.

 We say:

Section: The One He Watches

 Two metres past the herd's base, at the road edge. He faces across the road, not
 along it, like every other pig.

  gaze : Critter
  gaze = gaze-pig 1000.0 2.0

  gaze-got : List Real
  gaze-got = [gaze.along, gaze.across, gaze.height, pig-height, pig-dist-before-end, gaze-pig-along-offset]

  gaze-got-want : List Real
  gaze-got-want = [942.0, 12.0, 1.1, 1.1, 60.0, 2.0]

  gaze-kind-got : List Integer
  gaze-kind-got = [gaze.codepoint, pig-cp, pig-novelty-count, big-herd-cols, big-herd-rows]

  gaze-kind-want : List Integer
  gaze-kind-want = [128022, 128022, 2, 7, 7]

  gaze-face-got : List Boolean
  gaze-face-got = [gaze.face-right]

  gaze-face-want : List Boolean
  gaze-face-want = [False]

Section: The Big Herd

 Forty-nine, laid out row by row, seven to a row -- so index `r * 7 + c` is the
 order they come out in and the across value changes only every seventh animal.

  herd : List Critter
  herd = fill-pig-herd 1000.0

  herd-count-got : List Integer
  herd-count-got = [list-length herd, list-length (fill-pig-herd 500.0)]

  herd-count-want : List Integer
  herd-count-want = [49, 49]

 The first row and the last, along: each column is four further on, and the whole
 row has sheared six per row it is back.

  along-of : Integer, Integer -> Real
  along-of (r) (c) = (list-at herd (r * 7 + c)).along

  row-alongs : Integer -> List Real
  row-alongs (r) =
    [along-of r 0, along-of r 1, along-of r 2, along-of r 3, along-of r 4, along-of r 5, along-of r 6]

  herd-along-got : List Real
  herd-along-got = row-alongs 0 & row-alongs 3 & row-alongs 6

  herd-along-want : List Real
  herd-along-want =
    [ 934.0, 938.0, 942.0, 946.0, 950.0, 954.0, 958.0,
      952.0, 956.0, 960.0, 964.0, 968.0, 972.0, 976.0,
      970.0, 974.0, 978.0, 982.0, 986.0, 990.0, 994.0 ]

 Across depends on the ROW ONLY, so all seven in a row share a band and the seven
 bands are six apart. Taking one from each row is what shows that.

  herd-across-got : List Real
  herd-across-got =
    [ (list-at herd 0).across, (list-at herd 6).across,
      (list-at herd 7).across, (list-at herd 13).across,
      (list-at herd 14).across, (list-at herd 21).across,
      (list-at herd 28).across, (list-at herd 35).across,
      (list-at herd 42).across, (list-at herd 48).across ]

  herd-across-want : List Real
  herd-across-want = [12.0, 12.0, 18.0, 18.0, 24.0, 30.0, 36.0, 42.0, 48.0, 48.0]

  herd-kind-got : List Integer
  herd-kind-got = [(list-at herd 0).codepoint, (list-at herd 48).codepoint]

  herd-kind-want : List Integer
  herd-kind-want = [128022, 128022]

Section: The Straight Ranks

 Four at the road edge and six six metres further off, at written-down offsets
 either side of the base. No sine anywhere, so these are exact.

  row : List Critter
  row = fill-pig-row 1000.0

  row-count-got : List Integer
  row-count-got = [list-length row, list-length pig-row-front, list-length pig-row-back]

  row-count-want : List Integer
  row-count-want = [10, 4, 6]

  row-along-got : List Real
  row-along-got = list-map (\p -> p.along) row

  row-along-want : List Real
  row-along-want =
    [ 934.0, 938.0, 942.0, 946.0,
      930.0, 934.0, 938.0, 942.0, 946.0, 950.0 ]

  row-across-got : List Real
  row-across-got = list-map (\p -> p.across) row

  row-across-want : List Real
  row-across-want = [12.0, 12.0, 12.0, 12.0, 18.0, 18.0, 18.0, 18.0, 18.0, 18.0]

  offsets-got : List Real
  offsets-got = pig-row-front & pig-row-back & [pig-back-row-offset, pig-herd-first-col, pig-col-spacing, pig-row-depth, pig-jitter-along, pig-jitter-across]

  offsets-want : List Real
  offsets-want =
    [ -6.0, -2.0, 2.0, 6.0,
      -10.0, -6.0, -2.0, 2.0, 6.0, 10.0,
      6.0, -6.0, 4.0, 6.0, 1.2, 1.0 ]

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni (grade-reals "pg-gaze  " gaze-got gaze-got-want 0.0)
    print-line-uni (grade-ints  "pg-kind  " gaze-kind-got gaze-kind-want)
    print-line-uni (grade-bools "pg-face  " gaze-face-got gaze-face-want)
    print-line-uni (grade-ints  "pg-nherd " herd-count-got herd-count-want)
    print-line-uni (grade-ints  "pg-hkind " herd-kind-got herd-kind-want)
    print-line-uni (grade-ints  "pg-nrow  " row-count-got row-count-want)
    print-line-uni (grade-reals "pg-rowa  " row-along-got row-along-want 0.0)
    print-line-uni (grade-reals "pg-rowx  " row-across-got row-across-want 0.0)
    print-line-uni (grade-reals "pg-offs  " offsets-got offsets-want 0.0)
    print-line-uni (grade-reals "pg-herda " herd-along-got herd-along-want 1.2)
    print-line-uni (grade-reals "pg-herdx " herd-across-got herd-across-want 1.0)
  end
